        1536,
        1527
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "On December 22, 1988, the Mayor of the City of New York, with the support of Chancellor Richard R. Green and Board of Education President Robert F. Wagner, Jr., announced the establishment of the Joint Commission on Integrity in the Public Schools to investigate allegations of corruption and improprieties within the City School District of the City of New York. By this resolution, the Board of Education and the Chancellor direct all officers and employees of the City School District to cooperate fully with the Commission in its investigation.",
